menu "Prusa Remote Display button"

    config PRD_BUTTON_ENABLED
        bool "Initialise the multifunction button as product input"
        default y
        help
            Brings up the button and feeds its classified gestures into the
            application store, where app_core translates them into
            app_model::ButtonGesture facts and the reducer decides what they mean.

            This is product behaviour and belongs in every profile. It is separate
            from PRD_BUTTON_EVENT_LOG below, which only adds validation logging:
            until Milestone 2 Phase B the two were the same switch, so the only way
            to have a working button was to compile a bring-up flow into the image.

            Turning this off leaves the input uninitialised. Nothing else changes —
            the component compiles either way — but the device then has no physical
            input at all.

    config PRD_BUTTON_EVENT_LOG
        bool "Additionally log every classified gesture"
        depends on PRD_BUTTON_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Adds the Milestone 1 Phase E bring-up logging on top of normal product
            input: every classified gesture is logged with running per-gesture
            counters and the queue statistics, so presses can be counted against
            what the firmware actually classified.

            This is diagnostics, not product behaviour. Enable only in the
            hardware-validation profile; the debug and release profiles must leave
            it off so no validation code reaches a product image.

endmenu
